# Sync GitHub before edits

Before changing any project files (code, data, assets, config):

1. `git fetch origin` and check `git status` / `git log HEAD..origin/main` (or the current branch’s upstream).
2. If the local branch is behind remote, `git pull --ff-only` (or merge/rebase only if ff-only is not possible and the user asked).
3. Re-read the files you will edit from disk after pull so you work on the latest content.
4. Never overwrite or delete remote changes by pushing a stale local copy. If there are divergent local and remote commits, stop and reconcile with the user before forcing anything.
5. Do not use destructive git commands (`push --force`, hard reset) unless the user explicitly asks.

This applies every time work resumes on this repo, including mid-conversation after the user may have edited on GitHub.
